<title>ARMENIA: U.S. firm wins tender to upgrade Yerevan airport.</title>
<headline>U.S. firm wins tender to upgrade Yerevan airport.</headline>
<dateline>YEREVAN 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. construction company Bill Harbert International has won an international tender to modernise the main airport in Armenia's capital Yerevan, an airport official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Karen Mkhitaryan, director of the facility's international department, told Reuters that the company would construct a $27.8 million cargo terminal.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to increase the airport's cargo handling capacity to 80,000 tonnes a year from 50,000 tonnes,&quot; he said, adding that a final agreement would be signed next week.</p>
<p>Five other companies took part in the tender.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
